  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "We call a non-negative number xxx good if its binary representation is palindromic. For example, 107107107 is good because its binary representation is 110101111010111101011 which is palindromic while 101010 is not good because its binary representation is 101010101010 which is not palindromic.\n\nRecall that, a string is said to be palindromic if it reads the same backward as forward.\n\nYou are given a number nnn. You have to express nnn as a sum of at most 121212 good numbers. If there exist multiple answers, print any one of them.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each testcase contains a single integer nnn.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, print a single integer mmm (1≤m≤121 \\le m \\le 121≤m≤12), denoting the number of good numbers. In the next line, print a sequence of mmm good numbers whose sum is equal to nnn. If there are multiple such sequences, print any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤n≤10001 \\leq n \\leq 10001≤n≤1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n24\n4",
        "output": "2\n21 3\n4\n1 1 1 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\n212121 is good because 21=(10101)221 = (10101)_221=(10101)2​ which is palindromic.\n333 is good because 3=(11)23 = (11)_23=(11)2​ which is palindromic.\n\nTest case 222:\n\n111 is good because 1=(1)21 = (1)_21=(1)2​ which is palindromic.\n\nHere ()2()_2()2​ denotes binary representation of the number."
      }
    ]
  },
